  "live_records": {
    "q-279613": {
      "dom_id": "step-q279613",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $X∼B(6,0.3),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X=1)≈${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(6,0.3),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x})(0.3)^{x}(0.7)^{6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1) & =f(1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1})(0.3)^{1}(0.7)^{6-1} \\\\  & =6(0.3)^{1}(0.7)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.303\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
