    "q-279767": {
      "dom_id": "step-q279767",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "If $X∼B(5,0.1),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places** $P(0<X\\le 2)≈${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(5,0.1),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.1)^{x}(0.9)^{5-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1})(0.1)^{1}(0.9)^{5-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2})(0.1)^{2}(0.9)^{5-2} \\\\  & =5(0.1)^{1}(0.9)^{4}+10(0.1)^{2}(0.9)^{3} \\\\  & ≈0.401\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
